<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I8a40f0474efb1f62c6e20e82fc10bce7a4ceb7c8" commit="c0db9f25a5da58a8c639ee9c7942fb8cb3bd5a56" commit_message="webserver: move back to platform2  We aren't getting this from AOSP anymore.  BUG=chromium:788227 TEST=precq passes  Change-Id: I8a40f0474efb1f62c6e20e82fc10bce7a4ceb7c8 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/788456 Commit-Ready: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Mike Frysinger &lt;vapier@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Dan Erat &lt;derat@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="788456" owner_email="vapier@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/manifest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/manifest" ref="refs/changes/56/788456/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I4b6d798af4618cbd4179f8700ebb2aa78021207e" commit="314476c853a49c35fb09cae0ef67016ffd51c6de" commit_message="cannonlake: Check for hard and soft off in chipset_force_shutdown  Similar to CL:774298, intention of chipset_force_shutdown is to power off the AP by simulating power button press until it results in power button override and shuts down AP. However, if AP is already in hard or soft off conditions (i.e. G3, S5G3, G3S5 or S5) then AP is already off, and simulating power button press results in charge_prevent_power_on from incorrectly assuming that the power button is pressed by user. Thus, check if the system is in soft or hard off before shutting it down.  BUG=b:65864825 BRANCH=None TEST=make -j buildall  Change-Id: I4b6d798af4618cbd4179f8700ebb2aa78021207e Signed-off-by: Furquan Shaikh &lt;furquan@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/791933 Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="791933" owner_email="furquan@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/33/791933/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ifa89f8929987d86c9e02530b663d563dbe25ed85" commit="603786d5289dc84ec7c74cc790256b717eadcace" commit_message="intel_x86: Auto power-on after battery SOC is above minimum required  If power-up is inhibited by charger because of battery SOC, then check for the conditions again on BATTERY_SOC_CHANGE. This allows the EC to boot the AP up on connecting AC power and SOC going above the minimum required.  BUG=b:65864825 BRANCH=None TEST=Verified following on coral and soraka: 1. Discharge battery to ~0% 2. Connect AC power ==&gt; Power-up is inhibited 3. When battery SOC reaches 1%. AP is not taken out of reset: &quot;[12.974428 Battery 1% / 8h:4 to full] [12.980439 power-up still inhibited]&quot; 4. When battery SOC reaches 2%, AP is taken out of reset: &quot;[9.230148 Battery 2% / 4h:5 to full] [9.236122 Battery SOC ok to boot AP!]&quot;  Change-Id: Ifa89f8929987d86c9e02530b663d563dbe25ed85 Signed-off-by: Furquan Shaikh &lt;furquan@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/753294 Reviewed-by: Shawn N &lt;shawnn@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="753294" owner_email="furquan@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="7" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/94/753294/7" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ic548b911b7a7ae6544352e6a2ef0808e13fb1e30" commit="c200569531a6a7f80b4b75d9afc0f32cb16140d0" commit_message="installer: Stop printing source lsb-release in postinst  postinst should not try to print the source lsb-release because it does not have access to it. We will show the source lsb-release in the update_engine itself.  BUG=chromium:786225 TEST=cros flash and update_engine.log does not show the source lsb-release.  Change-Id: Ic548b911b7a7ae6544352e6a2ef